# Stack

**Recommended:** [Astro](https://astro.build) with the content collections
API and zero client JS by default. This matches the "quiet tools" ethos —
static HTML, hand-tunable, fast.

Other acceptable: Eleventy (11ty), Hugo, Next.js (App Router, RSC).
Hard-no on SPA frameworks for the public site: this is a reading site,
not an application.

## Project layout (Astro)

```
.
├── src/
│   ├── content/
│   │   ├── config.ts                # zod schemas for post types
│   │   └── posts/
│   │       ├── 2026-05-22-quietness-of-tools.mdx
│   │       └── …
│   ├── styles/
│   │   ├── tokens.css               # ← copy from handoff/tokens.css verbatim
│   │   └── components.css           # ← copy from handoff/reference/styles.css
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── Mast.astro
│   │   ├── Sidebar.astro
│   │   ├── Post.astro
│   │   ├── ArchiveRow.astro
│   │   ├── RateRow.astro
│   │   ├── AvailabilityCal.astro
│   │   ├── CTA.astro
│   │   └── SiteFooter.astro
│   ├── layouts/
│   │   ├── Base.astro               # html shell, fonts, meta, tokens import
│   │   └── PageWithSidebar.astro    # mast + grid + footer wrapper
│   └── pages/
│       ├── index.astro              # landing — pulls latest 10 posts
│       ├── archive.astro            # archive — all posts, grouped by year
│       ├── sponsor.astro            # sponsorship page (static markdown ok)
│       ├── feed.xml.ts              # atom feed
│       └── [year]/[month]/[slug].astro   # individual post
├── public/
│   ├── archive.txt                  # plain-text fallback index
│   └── …
├── astro.config.mjs
├── tsconfig.json
└── package.json
```

## Required Astro integrations

```bash
pnpm add -D @astrojs/mdx @astrojs/sitemap @astrojs/rss
```

- `@astrojs/mdx` — posts are MDX so you can embed the occasional component.
- `@astrojs/sitemap` — auto-sitemap for the canonical URL.
- `@astrojs/rss` (or Atom via `astro-rss-style`) — `/feed.xml` is mandatory.

## Build target

- Static output (`output: 'static'`).
- Deploy to Netlify, Vercel, or Cloudflare Pages.
- Ensure trailing-slash policy is consistent (recommended: `trailingSlash:
  'never'`).
- Set canonical URL in `astro.config.mjs` so feeds and sitemap come out
  with absolute hrefs.

## What NOT to add

- No client-side router. No Astro `<Image>` until there's an actual image
  asset to optimize.
- No analytics scripts. (If you must measure traffic, use a server-side
  log analyser like GoatCounter or Plausible's no-cookie embed — and put
  it in the site footer with a privacy note.)
- No comment system. The site is one-way.
- No Tailwind unless you also wire `tokens.json` into `theme.extend` so
  utilities resolve to tokens. Otherwise it competes with the token layer
  and devolves into hex codes in JSX.
